"Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Sheffield, S3 7RH, UK"}]},{"uuid":"a66474ef-35fa-4976-86f3-e5cd8f617380","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1066357"},"full_name":"Warner, D.","affiliations":[{"value":"Colorado State U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/902747"}}],"signature_block":"WARNARd","raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Physics, Colorado State University, Fort Collins, CO, 80523-1875, USA"}]},{"uuid":"a21eccbd-98fc-4eeb-b062-45ff22986825","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2338672"},"full_name":"Yuriev, L.","affiliations":[{"value":"Sheffield U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903196"}}],"signature_block":"YARAFl","raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Sheffield, S3 7RH, UK"}]}],"curated":true,"figures":[{"key":"f989965e7062e8eb1e06e98651739fbb","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/f989965e7062e8eb1e06e98651739fbb","source":"arxiv","caption":"a) Example minority carrier event in the right drift volume, which produced $4980$~NIPs at a distance of $35.6\\pm0.2$~cm from the right MWPC during a neutron run. In the waveform labels, `R' stands for `right', `A' for `anode', `G' for `grid', `V' for `veto' and `S' for `sum'. Horizontal gray lines above the colored anode waveforms indicate the analysis threshold. b) labeled detail of the channel RA7 (blue online) waveform before (grey) and after (black) application of the undershoot removal algorithm discussed in the text. The dotted vertical line separates the minority (S, P, D) peaks from the main (I) peak.","filename":"MinCarEventDisplay4.png"},{"key":"3d08eb6c96103933c6422f8c84fd218c","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/3d08eb6c96103933c6422f8c84fd218c","source":"arxiv","caption":"a) Example minority carrier event in the right drift volume, which produced $4980$~NIPs at a distance of $35.6\\pm0.2$~cm from the right MWPC during a neutron run. In the waveform labels, `R' stands for `right', `A' for `anode', `G' for `grid', `V' for `veto' and `S' for `sum'. Horizontal gray lines above the colored anode waveforms indicate the analysis threshold. b) labeled detail of the channel RA7 (blue online) waveform before (grey) and after (black) application of the undershoot removal algorithm discussed in the text. The dotted vertical line separates the minority (S, P, D) peaks from the main (I) peak.","filename":"MinCarExample4.png"},{"key":"d2f40cee5bed8058c5755a55f6b2551d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/d2f40cee5bed8058c5755a55f6b2551d","source":"arxiv","caption":"$z$ vs. NIPs distributions of events in the WIMP search and calibration neutron datasets. Events recorded during WIMP-search operation (left panel). No background events appear in the bulk fiducial volume at any energy and this permits the definition of a large background-free signal region below $z = 48.4$\\,cm, which is shown to be sensitive to neutron recoils, and hence WIMP interactions, by the calibration data (right panel). The grid lines are drawn to match the bins in the efficiency map of Figure~\\ref{fig:map}. The absence of events below $z \\sim 10$\\,cm and the $z$-dependence of the low-energy cutoff in the neutron calibration data are described in the text.","filename":"zNipsSideBySide2.png"},{"key":"056852092b9ade3272d8d2b47e31410b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/056852092b9ade3272d8d2b47e31410b","source":"arxiv","caption":"An efficiency map for recoil detection including all analysis cuts.  Each cell shows the number of detected recoils over the number expected from the GEANT4 simulation.","filename":"EfficiencyMapColour6.png"},{"key":"bc03680f1932cb41d381ef6945bb8cb6","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/bc03680f1932cb41d381ef6945bb8cb6","source":"arxiv","caption":"Limits on the spin-dependent WIMP-proton interaction cross section. Limits obtained from these data are shown in black, and the previous limit curve from the DRIFT experiment using a similar live time is shown in grey~\\cite{Daw2012}. All limits from other directional DM detectors (DMTPC~\\cite{Ahlen2011} and NEWAGE~\\cite{Miuchi2010}) are also shown. The leading non-directional detector limits are also shown (PICASSO~\\cite{Archambault2012}, SIMPLE~\\cite{Felizardo2012} and COUPP~\\cite{Behnke2012}).","filename":"Limits5.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["DRIFT:2014bny","Battat:2014van"],"citeable":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2016-06-14"}],"keywords":[{"value":"Dark matter","source":"author"},{"value":"Time projection chamber","source":"author"},{"value":"DRIFT","source":"author"},{"value":"detector: upgrade","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"ion: negative particle","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"spin: dependence","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"dark matter: detector","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"time projection chamber","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"gas","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"nucleus: recoil","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"WIMP p","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"WIMP: direct detection","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"efficiency","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"The addition of O 2 to gas mixtures in time projection chambers containing CS 2 has recently been shown to produce multiple negative ions that travel at slightly different velocities. This allows a measurement of the absolute position of ionising events in the z  (drift) direction. In this work, we apply the z -fiducialisation technique to a directional dark matter search. We present results from a 46.3 live-day source-free exposure of the DRIFT-IId detector run in this new mode. With full-volume fiducialisation, we have achieved the first background-free operation of a directional detector. The resulting exclusion curve for spin-dependent WIMP-proton interactions reaches 1.1 pb at 100 GeV/c 2 , a factor of 2 better than our previous work. We describe the automated analysis used here, and argue that detector upgrades, implemented after the acquisition of these data, will bring an additional factor of ≳3 improvement in the near future.","source":"Elsevier"},{"value":"The addition of O2 to gas mixtures in time projection chambers containing CS2 has recently been shown to produce multiple negative ions that travel at slightly different velocities. This allows a measurement of the absolute position of ionising events in the z (drift) direction. In this work, we apply the z-fiducialisation technique to a directional dark matter search. In particular, we present results from a 46.3 live-day source-free exposure of the DRIFT-IId detector run in this completely new mode. With full-volume fiducialisation, we have achieved the first background-free operation of a directional detector. The resulting exclusion curve for spin-dependent WIMP-proton interactions reaches 1.1 pb at 100 GeV/c2, a factor of 2 better than our previous work. We describe the automated analysis used here, and argue that detector upgrades, implemented after the acquisition of these data, will bring an additional factor of >3 improvement in the near future.","source":"arXiv"}],"copyright":[{"statement":"Copyright © unknown. Published by Elsevier B.V."}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1126428"},"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevD.86.010001"],"misc":["P. a. Zyla, C. Amsler, M. Antonelli, D. M. Asner, H. Baer, H. R. Band, T. Basaglia, C. W Bauer, Review of particle physics URL"],"label":"1","authors":[{"full_name":"Beringer, J."},{"full_name":"Arguin, J.F."},{"full_name":"Barnett, R.M."},{"full_name":"Copic, K."},{"full_name":"Dahl, O."},{"full_name":"Groom, D.E."},{"full_name":"Lin, C.J."},{"full_name":"Lys, J."},{"full_name":"Murayama, H."},{"full_name":"Wohl, C.G."},{"full_name":"Yao, W.M."}],"publication_info":{"year":2012,"artid":"010001","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"86"}},"curated_relation":false},{"reference":{"misc":["Dark Matter C